msgid "The BigBlueButton API calls are almost all made server-to-server. If you installed the package bbb-demo on your BigBlueButton server, you get a set of API examples, written in Java Server Pages (JSP), that demonstrate how to use the BigBlueButton API. These demos run as a web application in tomcat7. The web application makes HTTPS requests to the BigBlueButton server’s API end point."
msgstr "Le chiamate API di BigBlueButton vengono quasi tutte effettuate da server a server. Se hai installato il pacchetto bbb-demo sul tuo server BigBlueButton, ottieni un set di esempi API, scritti in Java Server Pages (JSP), che dimostrano come utilizzare l'API BigBlueButton. Queste demo vengono eseguite come applicazione web in tomcat7. L'applicazione web effettua richieste HTTPS all'endpoint API del server BigBlueButton."

msgid "The BigBlueButton API security model enables 3rd-party applications to make API calls (if they have the shared secret), but not allow other people (end users) to make API calls."
msgstr "Il modello di sicurezza dell'API BigBlueButton consente alle applicazioni di terze parti di effettuare chiamate API (se dispongono del segreto condiviso), ma non consente ad altre persone (utenti finali) di effettuare chiamate API."

msgid "The BigBlueButton API security model enables 3rd-party applications to make API calls (if they have the shared secret), but not allow other people (end users) to make API calls.\n\n\t\t\t\t\tThe BigBlueButton API calls are almost all made server-to-server. If you installed the package bbb-demo on your BigBlueButton server, you get a set of API examples, written in Java Server Pages (JSP), that demonstrate how to use the BigBlueButton API. These demos run as a web application in tomcat7. The web application makes HTTPS requests to the BigBlueButton server’s API end point.\n\n\t\t\t\t\tYou can retrieve your BigBlueButton API parameters (API endpoint and shared secret) using the command\n\n\t\t\t\t\t$ bbb-conf --secret"
msgstr ""

